# Home page. Core's wording invites the visitor to make a request. This site
# has one requester, so the same slots describe the archive instead.
# Homepage wording reviewed by the owner.

msgid "Your right to know"
msgstr "An archive of Freedom of Information requests"

msgid "Every citizen has the right to access information held by public authorities."
msgstr "Requests to public bodies asking for information, and their replies, published in full."

msgid "By law, they have to respond."
msgstr "Public bodies have to answer by law."

msgid "How it works"
msgstr "How this works"

msgid "You have the <strong>right</strong> to request information from any publicly-funded body, and get answers. {{site_name}} helps you make a Freedom of Information request. It also publishes all requests online."
msgstr "Everyone has the <strong>right</strong> to ask a public body for the information it holds. This is a record of requests that have been made, and the information that was released."

msgid "Use this site to make your request for information – we'll show you how."
msgstr "A request for information is sent to a public body by email."

msgid "We'll drop you an email as soon as your request gets a response."
msgstr "The authority replies. By law it normally has 20 working days."

msgid "We publish it all online. Great! Now you have your answer, and everybody else can access it too."
msgstr "Selected requests are published here in full."

msgid "Learn more &rarr;"
msgstr "About this site &rarr;"

msgid "Who can I request information from?"
msgstr "Authorities"

msgid "{{site_name}} covers requests to {{number_of_authorities}} authority, including:"
msgid_plural "{{site_name}} covers requests to {{number_of_authorities}} authorities, including:"
msgstr[0] "{{number_of_authorities}} authority is listed:"
msgstr[1] "{{number_of_authorities}} authorities are listed, including:"

msgid "What information has been requested?"
msgstr "Latest requests"

msgid "What information has been released?"
msgstr "Latest requests"

msgid "{{site_name}} users have made {{number_of_requests}} request, including:"
msgid_plural "{{site_name}} users have made {{number_of_requests}} requests, including:"
msgstr[0] "{{number_of_requests}} request published so far:"
msgstr[1] "{{number_of_requests}} requests published so far, including:"

# Private by default. Core assumes everything is public the moment it is
# sent; on this site a request and its replies are private until the owner
# publishes them.

# Notices on things that are not published. Core's default explanation
# ("There are various reasons why we might have done this") reads as if a
# moderator had hidden something. Here, unpublished is the normal state.

# The daily summary email. Core's subject names Alaveteli Pro
# (PRO_SITE_NAME); here every account gets the summary
# (lib/model_patches.rb).

msgid "Your daily request summary from {{pro_site_name}}"
msgstr "Your daily request summary"

